      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after George Dole Wadley, a railroad official overseeing the construction of the line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/wadley/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The principal landmark of Wadley is Southern Union College, founded in 1922 by the Congregational Christian Church and originally called Bethlehem College.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
